---
title: "New RawTherapee 5.4 AppImage"
date: Aug 31 2018 19:12
author: DrSlony
---


<div id="article_show_text"><p>Linux users whose distributions do not ship RawTherapee 5.4 can now enjoy our latest stable release by getting the RawTherapee 5.4 AppImage from our Downloads page.</p>

<a name="lead_end"></a>

<p>An AppImage is a single file which contains all the components necessary to run a program in any Linux distribution. As some distributions provide old versions of certain programs, the AppImage is a great solution for letting users of those systems run the latest version of a given program.</p>

<p>All you need to do after downloading it is to make it executable and run it:</p>
<pre style="margin-left: 4em;">chmod +x RawTherapee-releases-5.4.AppImage
./RawTherapee-releases-5.4.AppImage</pre></div>

